# Module Database Placement (mandatory)

## Rule

**New migrations and seeders go in the owning module**, not `database/migrations/` or `database/seeders/`.

| Asset | Location |
|-------|----------|
| Domain migrations | `Modules/{Name}/database/migrations/` |
| Domain seeders | `Modules/{Name}/database/seeders/` |
| Laravel framework (`0001_01_01_*` users, cache, queue jobs, sanctum tokens) | `Modules/Authentication/` + `Modules/Administration/` |
| Root orchestrator | `Modules/Administration/database/seeders/DatabaseSeeder.php` (`Database\Seeders` namespace via composer) |

## ServiceProvider

Every module with migrations must call in `boot()`:

```php
use Modules\Administration\app\Infrastructure\Migration\RegistersModuleMigrations;

class ExampleServiceProvider extends ServiceProvider
{
    use RegistersModuleMigrations;

    public function boot(): void
    {
        $this->loadModuleMigrations('Example');
    }
}
```

## Distribute existing shared files

```bash
php artisan migration:distribute-to-modules --move --seeders --force
```

Per-module legacy collectors still work:

```bash
php artisan clinics:collect-migrations
php artisan ecommerce:collect-migrations
php artisan inventory:collect-migrations
```

## Never

- `migrate:fresh` on shared PostgreSQL
- Duplicate the same migration in `database/migrations/` AND `Modules/{Name}/database/migrations/`

Audit: `docs/refactoring/MODULE_AUDIT.md`
